                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On September 6, 1953, Prime Minister Ghazi resigned and Prince Mohammed Daud formed a new government in which
                    the former Ambassador to the United States, Mohammed
                        Naim, became the Foreign Minister.</p>
            </div>
